@tvernum I have tried to reproduce the scenario and tend to think it was indeed a network problem. When at startup (unless security is explicitly disabled) we always add a default header `DefaultAuthenticationFailureHandler` to:
`if (failureResponseHeaders == null || failureResponseHeaders.isEmpty()) {
            this.defaultFailureResponseHeaders = Collections.singletonMap("WWW-Authenticate",
                       Collections.singletonList("Basic realm=\"" + XPackField.SECURITY + "\" charset=\"UTF-8\""));
 }`
We also add Realms dispite the current license and always add default ones.
I tried upgrading both from Trial and Basic to Gold and everything works properly - authentication dialog pops up after upgrade.
